th  chicken breast  beef big beans  or any other protein of your choice try  it out the next student meal is white  bean chicken soup this is a one pot dish  so it is as simple as dumping all the  ingredients into a pot and allow them to  cook so for my recipe I'm using one can  of white beans rinsed and drained when  chicken breast 2 onions 4 celery stalks  1 carrot 1 tomato about 4 cups of  chicken stock quarter teaspoon of mixed  herbs and salt and pepper to taste so  start by prepping all your ingredients  chop up all the vegetables the next step  is to simply fill up a pot with chicken  stock and add in all your ingredients so  I'm seasoning mine with a little bit of  mixed herbs and also salt and pepper now  allow all the ingredients to cook under  medium heat for 15 minutes or until the  chicken is cooked through and vegetables  are tender serve warm what I love about  this recipe is that you can use  different meats or beans and pick your  favorite vegetables and it is a one pot  dish that is packed with nutrients plus  you will have less washing to do so each  stuffing has about 343 calories I like  to cook this recipe in bulk and store  the extra in the fridge and warm them up  the next day and they will taste even  better my final favorite is black beans  salsa wrap this recipe does not require  any cooking so if your accommodation  doesn't allow you to cook you can try  this out  the ingredients you'll need are 1 can of  black beans 1 can of corn 1 red bell  pepper chopped 3 tablespoons of salsa  sauce 3 tablespoons of cheese 2 cups of  spinach 1/2 a teaspoon of mixed herbs  and 4 whole grain wraps in a bowl simply  combine the beans corn bell pepper salsa  sauce and season with mixed herbs now  let's assemble it arrange a handful of  spinach then spoon the bean mixture onto  the wrap and I'm going to top mine with  a little bit of shredded cheese roll it  up if you're a vegan you can simply omit  the cheese and to pack more vegetables  into your meal serve it with a side of  salad so this is a curve  by lunch to go and I used to take this  to uni with me each serving has under  300 calories you can even swap the rap  for pita bread or lettuce leaves so  these are some of my favourite lazy  student meals what I use let me know in  the comments below I hope this video  will encourage you to start to eat  better don't be like me when I was a  student okay start to learn to look  after yourself and your body will thank  you  long-term be sure to like this video  share this video on and subscribe to my  youtube channel for a lot more easy lazy  healthy recipes fitness videos and also  fitness tips all the best and start  cooking
 

